           <li>{{ group.grouper }}: {{ group.list|join(", ") }}
         {% endfor %}</ul>
 
+    ``key_transform`` is an optional callable that is applied to each
+    group key before it is yielded as ``grouper``. Only the displayed
+    key changes, the items are still grouped and sorted by the original
+    attribute value. This is useful to format keys such as dates.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        {% for month, posts in posts|groupby("date", key_transform=fmt) %}
+          <li>{{ month }}: {{ posts|map(attribute="title")|join(", ") }}</li>
+        {% endfor %}
+
+    .. versionadded:: 3.1
+        The ``key_transform`` parameter.
+
     You can specify a ``default`` value to use if an object in the list
     does not have the given attribute.
 
@@ -1203,6 +1219,18 @@ def sync_do_groupby(
           <li>{{ city }}: {{ items|map(attribute="name")|join(", ") }}</li>
         {% endfor %}</ul>
 
+    Groups are sorted in ascending order by default. Pass
+    ``reverse=True`` to sort them in descending order instead.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        <ul>{% for year, items in posts|groupby("year", reverse=true) %}
+          <li>{{ year }}: {{ items|map(attribute="title")|join(", ") }}</li>
+        {% endfor %}</ul>
+
+    .. versionchanged:: 3.1
+        Added the ``reverse`` parameter.
+
     .. versionchanged:: 3.0
         Added the ``default`` parameter.
 
